§§ `EXPECTED TO FAIL (4): what the regulation names is not what the Law now names`

-- (1) the column: reg 1 says E, the Law says D.
#ASSERT `the column of Schedule J that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` EQUALS `the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(3) has named since 1 January 2006`
-- (2) the threshold in reg 1: half the average wage, where the Law said 60% from 1 January 2006 ...
#ASSERT `the threshold that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` EQUALS `the threshold that s 342(e)(3) named from 1 January 2006 to 31 December 2025`
-- (3) ... and says the reduced collection threshold from 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `the threshold that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` EQUALS `the threshold that s 342(e)(3) names from 1 January 2026`
-- (4) the threshold in reg 2, which cites s 342(e)(3) itself.
#ASSERT `the threshold that reg 2 of 5757-1997 names` EQUALS `the threshold that s 342(e)(3) names from 1 January 2026`

§§ `Checks that pass, to show the comparison can pass and that the failures above are the regulation's drift`

-- When it was made (1997) the regulation named what the Law named, and the column it named was the employee's deduction column.
#ASSERT `the column of Schedule J that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` EQUALS `the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(3) named when the regulations were made`
#ASSERT `the threshold that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` EQUALS `the threshold that s 342(e)(3) named when the regulations were made`
#ASSERT `the column of Schedule J that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` EQUALS `the column of Schedule J headed the deduction from the employee's wage, as enacted in 1995`
-- The Law's s 342(e)(3) now names the deduction column; the column reg 1 names is now the Treasury allocation.
#ASSERT `the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(3) has named since 1 January 2006` EQUALS `the column of Schedule J headed the deduction from the employee's wage, as now printed`
#ASSERT `the column of Schedule J that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` EQUALS `the column of Schedule J headed the State Treasury's allocation under s 32(c1), as now printed`

§ `The 1999 amendment of the regulations: three citations of "regulation 3B" where the request for a refund is regulation 3C`

-- THE SECOND FINDING (added 2026-11-09, after the first; Kovetz HaTakanot 5956, 25.2.1999, pp. 440-441, in force from 13 Tevet 5759, 1.1.1999,
-- made under ss 342(e) and 400 of the Law). The amendment adds regs 3A, 3B and 3C and replaces reg 4. Reg 3B says reg 3A applies to a worker of a
-- "recognised employer"; reg 3C is the insured person's request for a refund of contributions deducted in excess. Reg 4(b) as replaced, twice,
-- and the words that the amendment's own reg 5 inserts into reg 6(a), name "regulation 3B" (the latter "section 3B") for the request for a refund.
-- The request for a refund is regulation 3C. The consolidation's editor marked all three with a "should read 3C" note (lines 48 and 54
-- of the regulations' deposited text); the page image shows the print itself says 3B, so the consolidation is faithful and the error is in the instrument.
-- Read literally, the Institute's duty in reg 6(a) to refund attaches to a request "under 3B", which is not a request for anything, and not to the reg 3C
-- request; a court would read 3C. The finding is about the text; the tier is PUBLIC and the severity low. The fix is one word in three places.
-- This module's other findings, and the answers the rules give, are unchanged: the rules of this row (nii-s342e-several-employers.l4) encode reg 3C.
-- The Hebrew below is transcribed from the page image of Kovetz HaTakanot 5956 p. 441 (takanot-5956-amend-5759-pp440-441-extract.pdf, PDF page 2), by hand:
-- ext:[KT5956-p441] | 3ב. תקנה 3א תחול לגבי עובד המועסק על ידי מעביד מוכר אם המציא העובד למעבידו כאמור פרטים על הכנסותיו.   [margin heading: עובד אצל מעביד מוכר]
-- ext:[KT5956-p441] | 3ג. מבוטח העובד אצל מעבידים שונים שנוכו משכרו דמי ביטוח בסכום העולה על דמי הביטוח המתואמים, יגיש למוסד בקשה להחזר דמי ביטוח, ...   [margin heading: בקשה להחזר דמי ביטוח ששולמו ביתר]
-- ext:[KT5956-p441] | (ב) מעביד ימסור לעובדו החייב להגיש דין וחשבון לפי תקנת משנה (א), או המגיש בקשה לפי תקנה 3ב, בתום שנת הדיווח או בתום התקופה שלגביה מבקש העובד להגיש בקשה לפי תקנה 3ב, לפי הענין, אישור ...
-- ext:[KT5956-p441] | 5. בתקנה 6(א) לתקנות העיקריות, אחרי ״דין וחשבון לפי תקנה 4״ בא ״או בקשה להחזר דמי ביטוח לפי סעיף 3ב״.
-- ext:[reg-several] 48 | ... או המגיש בקשה לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 3ג|תקנה 3ב {{ח:הערה|[צ״ל: 3ג]}}}}, ...   (the consolidation's own note, expanded)

DECLARE `A regulation added to the regulations of 5757-1997 in 1999` IS ONE OF
    `regulation 3A`
    `regulation 3B`
    `regulation 3C`

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(b) as replaced, first citation (Kovetz HaTakanot 5956 p. 441; reg line 48)
GIVETH A `A regulation added to the regulations of 5757-1997 in 1999`
`the regulation that reg 4(b) cites first for a request for a refund` MEANS `regulation 3B`

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(b) as replaced, second citation (Kovetz HaTakanot 5956 p. 441; reg line 48)
GIVETH A `A regulation added to the regulations of 5757-1997 in 1999`
`the regulation that reg 4(b) cites second for a request for a refund` MEANS `regulation 3B`

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) as amended by reg 5 of the 1999 amendment (Kovetz HaTakanot 5956 p. 441; reg line 54)
GIVETH A `A regulation added to the regulations of 5757-1997 in 1999`
`the regulation that the words inserted into reg 6(a) cite for a request for a refund` MEANS `regulation 3B`

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3C, margin heading "request for a refund of contributions paid in excess" (Kovetz HaTakanot 5956 p. 441)
GIVETH A `A regulation added to the regulations of 5757-1997 in 1999`
`the regulation whose heading is the request for a refund of contributions paid in excess` MEANS `regulation 3C`

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3B, margin heading "a worker of a recognised employer" (Kovetz HaTakanot 5956 p. 441)
GIVETH A `A regulation added to the regulations of 5757-1997 in 1999`
`the regulation whose heading is a worker of a recognised employer` MEANS `regulation 3B`

§§ `EXPECTED TO FAIL (3): the citations name regulation 3B where the request for a refund is regulation 3C`

-- (5) reg 4(b), first citation.
#ASSERT `the regulation that reg 4(b) cites first for a request for a refund` EQUALS `the regulation whose heading is the request for a refund of contributions paid in excess`
-- (6) reg 4(b), second citation.
#ASSERT `the regulation that reg 4(b) cites second for a request for a refund` EQUALS `the regulation whose heading is the request for a refund of contributions paid in excess`
-- (7) the words reg 5 of the 1999 amendment inserts into reg 6(a).
#ASSERT `the regulation that the words inserted into reg 6(a) cite for a request for a refund` EQUALS `the regulation whose heading is the request for a refund of contributions paid in excess`

§§ `Checks that pass, to show the comparison can pass`

-- The three citations name the regulation headed "a worker of a recognised employer" (they name something that exists, and it is not a request).
#ASSERT `the regulation that reg 4(b) cites first for a request for a refund` EQUALS `the regulation whose heading is a worker of a recognised employer`
#ASSERT `the regulation that reg 4(b) cites second for a request for a refund` EQUALS `the regulation whose heading is a worker of a recognised employer`
#ASSERT `the regulation that the words inserted into reg 6(a) cite for a request for a refund` EQUALS `the regulation whose heading is a worker of a recognised employer`
#ASSERT NOT (`the regulation whose heading is a worker of a recognised employer` EQUALS `the regulation whose heading is the request for a refund of contributions paid in excess`)

§ `The corrigendum of 26 August 1997: reg 1 "coordinated contributions" cites s 342(d)(1), not s 432(d)(1)`

-- Kovetz HaTakanot 5848, 26.8.1997, p. 1112 (takanot-5848-corrigendum-5757-p1112-extract.pdf, PDF page 1), a correction of a printing error,
-- read from the page image: in the regulations of 5757-1997 as published in Kovetz HaTakanot 5835 p. 864, in reg 1, in the definition of
-- "coordinated contributions" ("דמי ביטוח מתואמים"), instead of "בסעיף 432(ד)(1)" it should read "בסעיף 342(ד)(1)".
-- It does not touch the definition of the full rate, the column or the threshold. The deposited consolidation of the regulations has the corrected
-- citation (reg line 16, quoted at nii-s342e-several-employers.l4 line 82), and this row takes the coordinated contributions as an input
-- (computed by row IL-05 from s 342(d)(1)). These checks pass; they type the correction so that a reader can see which citation is the one in force.
-- ext:[KT5848-p1112] | בתקנות הביטוח הלאומי (תשלום וניכוי דמי ביטוח משכר מבוטח העובד אצל מעבידים שונים), התשנ״ז-1997, שפורסמו בקובץ התקנות 5835, התשנ״ז, עמ׳ 864, בתקנה 1, בהגדרה ״דמי ביטוח מתואמים״, במקום ״בסעיף 432(ד)(1)״ צריך להיות ״בסעיף 342(ד)(1)״.

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 1, "coordinated contributions", as first printed (Kovetz HaTakanot 5835 p. 864)
GIVETH A STRING
`the section of the Law that reg 1 cited for coordinated contributions, as first printed` MEANS "432(d)(1)"

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 1, "coordinated contributions", as corrected (Kovetz HaTakanot 5848 p. 1112)
GIVETH A STRING
`the section of the Law that reg 1 cites for coordinated contributions, as corrected` MEANS "342(d)(1)"

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 1, "coordinated contributions", as the deposited consolidation prints it (reg line 16)
GIVETH A STRING
`the section of the Law that reg 1 cites for coordinated contributions, in the consolidation` MEANS "342(d)(1)"

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(d)(1), the definition of the coordinated contributions (row IL-05)
GIVETH A STRING
`the section of the Law that defines the coordinated contributions` MEANS "342(d)(1)"

#ASSERT `the section of the Law that reg 1 cites for coordinated contributions, as corrected` EQUALS `the section of the Law that defines the coordinated contributions`
#ASSERT `the section of the Law that reg 1 cites for coordinated contributions, in the consolidation` EQUALS `the section of the Law that reg 1 cites for coordinated contributions, as corrected`
#ASSERT NOT (`the section of the Law that reg 1 cited for coordinated contributions, as first printed` EQUALS `the section of the Law that defines the coordinated contributions`)
